{"step_index":1892,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:26:37Z","input_tokens":3054,"cache_read_tokens":131150,"output_tokens":3007,"content":"A dedicated **[📊 Tax & ITR Filing]** dashboard tab has been implemented alongside the existing **[🧾 Invoice Math Audit]** tab, providing a customizable, deterministic tax engine with shared reactive state.\n\n---\n\n### Key Implementations\n\n#### 1. Tab Navigation Bar ([`ReviewWorkspace.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/ReviewWorkspace.js))\n- Added an interactive tab switcher directly above the review layout:\n  - **Tab 1: [🧾 Invoice Math Audit]**: Shows the live audit badge (e.g. `Math Verified & Valid` or `₹X Overcharge`).\n  - **Tab 2: [📊 Tax & ITR Filing]**: Displays the new compliance & tax planning dashboard with `Custom Engine` badge.\n- **Tab 1 Preserved Untouched:** The PDF/image preview, bounding boxes, interactive line-item table, math discrepancy engine, GST split inputs, quick rate buttons, and mobile views remain untouched.\n- **Shared Reactive State:** Updates in Tab 1 (such as editing billed amounts or GST splits) immediately reflect in Tab 2's ITC metrics and COGS auto-fill. Likewise, adjusting tax parameters in Tab 2 updates calculations live without losing state.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Customizable Tax & ITR Engine ([`taxCalculator.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js), [`TaxFilingDashboard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/TaxFilingDashboard.js))\n\n##### A. Regime & Filing Scheme Selector\n- **Tax Regime Toggle:** Switch dynamically between **[New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC - Default)]** and **[Old Tax Regime]**.\n- **Mode A: \"Regular Business (Normal P&L - ITR-3)\"**:\n  - Inputs for:\n    - **Annual Gross Revenue / Sales (₹)**\n    - **Cost of Goods Sold (Purchases)** with a 1-click **`[⚡ Auto-fill from Current Bill (₹X)]`** helper or custom manual input.\n    - **Other Operating Expenses (Rent, Power, Salaries, Misc) (₹)**.\n  - Computes: $\\text{Net Taxable Profit} = \\max(0, \\text{Gross Revenue} - \\text{Total Expenses})$.\n- **Mode B: \"Presumptive Taxation (Sec\n<truncated 1764 bytes>\nT (₹)**.\n- **Business Resale Toggle:**\n  - **`[Yes]`**: Flags as **`100% Eligible ITC for GSTR-3B Set-off`** (subject to valid supplier GSTIN under Section 16).\n  - **`[No]`**: Flags as **`Ineligible / Blocked Credit under Sec 17(5)`** (personal consumption, motor vehicles, or food/beverages).\n- **Net Cash GST Outflow Estimator:**\n  - Enter expected Gross Output GST collected from retail sales.\n  - Subtracts eligible purchase ITC to compute **Net Payable GST in Cash** and highlights direct cash saved.\n\n##### E. 1-Click Export\n- **`[📥 Download Tax & ITC Sheet (CSV)]`**: Generates a UTF-8 BOM CSV containing invoice details, regime and scheme configuration, profit breakdown, deductions claimed, slab-by-slab tax, and ITC cash flow.\n- **`[🖨️ Print / PDF]`**: Triggers a print-ready view formatted for Chartered Accountants (CA) with unneeded UI buttons hidden.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Summary\n\n1. **Deterministic Test Suite:**\n   - **Mode B Presumptive (Turnover ₹36L, 60% Digital @ 6%, 40% Cash @ 8%):**\n     - Digital Profit: ₹1,29,600 | Cash Profit: ₹1,15,200 | Deemed Profit: ₹2,44,800\n     - Net Taxable Income: ₹1,69,800 (after ₹75,000 standard deduction)\n     - Sec 87A full rebate applied: **₹0 Tax Payable** (100% verified)\n   - **Mode A Regular P&L (Turnover ₹50L, COGS ₹30L, Opex ₹5L):**\n     - Profit: ₹15,00,000 | Taxable: ₹14,25,000 | Slabs + 4% Cess: ₹1,30,000\n     - Blocked ITC under Sec 17(5) verified when toggle is set to `No`.\n2. **Module & Asset Serving:**\n   - All components ([`TaxFilingDashboard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/TaxFilingDashboard.js), [`ReviewWorkspace.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/ReviewWorkspace.js), [`taxCalculator.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js), [`app.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/app.js)) tested and served with HTTP 200 on [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).","thinking":"The prompt requires a tabbed navigation bar within the invoice review view. The existing component needs to be updated to include two tabs: \"Invoice Math Audit\" (the current view) and a new \"Tax & ITR Filing\" tab. The implementation should be within the specified JavaScript file.\n\n\nThe existing invoice review component needs tabbed navigation. The first tab, \"Invoice Math Audit\", will retain its current functionality, sourcing from existing JavaScript files.\n\nA new \"Tax & ITR Filing\" tab requires a customizable tax engine. This includes a regime and filing type selector allowing for both new and old tax regimes, with two filing modes. Mode A calculates net taxable profit based on gross revenue and expenses, while Mode B offers a presumptive taxation approach with customizable digital/cash percentages.\n\n\nThe \"Tax & ITR Filing\" tab requires detailed tax computation logic. It needs a revenue calculation based on digital and cash sales with customizable percentages.  Custom deduction fields are needed based on the tax regime, with standard deductions auto-applied for the new regime. A dynamic tax slab engine will compute and display tax breakdowns, including cess and effective tax rates.\n\nFurther requirements include a GST Input Tax Credit (ITC) audit that checks eligibility and estimates net GST outflow.  Finally, a one-click export will provide a downloadable tax computation sheet. This will all be implemented within the specified JavaScript file.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1893,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:33:55Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nINTEGRATION: WIRE TAB 2 (TAX & ITR FILING) INTO APP.JS WITH REACTIVE TAB SWITCHER\n\nConnect the newly created `TaxAndITRTab` component into `app.js` with a top-level tab switcher.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. COMPONENT IMPORT (app.js):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nImport the new component at the top of `app.js`:\nimport TaxAndITRTab from './components/TaxAndITRTab'; // Ensure path matches your structure\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. STATE MANAGEMENT (app.js):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdd an active tab state hook inside the main App component:\nconst [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('audit'); // 'audit' | 'tax'\n\nEnsure the active tab defaults to 'audit' upon uploading a new bill or resetting.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. TOP NAVIGATION SWITCHER BAR:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlace this tab switcher bar immediately below the top header / action bar and above the main content area (visible whenever an invoice has been loaded/parsed):\n\n<div className=\"flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-200 px-6 pt-3 bg-white\">\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    onClick={() => setActiveTab('audit')}\n    className={`pb-3 px-4 text-sm font-semibold flex items-center gap-2 border-b-2 transition-colors ${\n      activeTab === 'audit'\n        ? 'border-indigo-600 text-indigo-600'\n        : 'border-transparent text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-800'\n    }`}\n  >\n    <span>🧾</span>\n    <span>Invoice Math Audit</span>\n  </button>\n\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    onClick={() => setActiveTab('tax')}\n    className={`pb-3 px-4 text-sm font-semibold flex items-center gap-2 border-b-2 transition-colors ${\n      activeTab === 'tax'\n        ? 'border-indigo-600 text-indigo-600'\n        : 'border-transpare\n<truncated 14998 bytes>\nf req.digital_share_percent >= 95.0 else req.annual_turnover > 20000000.0\n        msg = \"Presumptive scheme elected. No formal profit & loss or balance sheet required under Section 44AB.\"\n    else:\n        taxable_income = max(0.0, req.annual_turnover - req.operating_expenses)\n        itr_form = \"ITR-3\"\n        tax_audit = req.annual_turnover > 10000000.0\n        msg = \"Regular business filing. Maintain vouchers, purchase invoices, and expense registers.\"\n\n    taxable_income = round(taxable_income, 2)\n\n    # 3. Tax Slabs (New Tax Regime FY 2025-26 / 2026-27 with Sec 87A rebate)\n    # Under New Regime, income up to 7 Lakhs (or extended limits) gets full 87A rebate\n    rebate_eligible = taxable_income <= 700000.0\n    projected_tax = 0.0 if rebate_eligible else round(taxable_income * 0.10, 2)\n\n    return TaxCalculationResponse(\n        total_itc=total_itc,\n        is_inter_state=is_inter_state,\n        gstin_valid=gstin_valid,\n        itc_compliance_notes=itc_notes,\n        taxable_business_income=taxable_income,\n        projected_income_tax=projected_tax,\n        rebate_87a_applied=rebate_eligible,\n        tax_audit_required=tax_audit,\n        itr_form_suggested=itr_form,\n        compliance_message=msg\n    )\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. ROUTE REGISTRATION:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIn your main FastAPI app (`main.py`):\nfrom routes.tax_advisory import router as tax_router # or include directly\napp.include_router(tax_router)\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSCOPE GUARD:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDO NOT change existing invoice parsing routes, Gemini model calls, or client-side privacy masking endpoints. Simply register this new `/api/tax/calculate-advisory` route alongside existing endpoints.\n\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-03T02:03:55+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
